{
	"nodes": [
		{
			"id": "header",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## Clinical Psychiatry and Psychopathology\n\nDomain hub: how psychopathology is described and classified, the main construct families, and the limits of assessment and evidence.\n\n[[Clinical Psychiatry and Psychopathology Map|Open the domain map]] - snapshot of 2026-09-27; the map's *In this folder* section is the live view.",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 0,
			"width": 2190,
			"height": 170,
			"color": "#F2C14E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_0",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Symptoms syndromes and diagnoses]]**\n*framework* - 5 sources\n\nThe levels of clinical description: individual symptoms, clusters that co-occur, and the diagnostic labels built on them.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 360,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 178,
			"color": "#F2C14E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Categorical versus dimensional classification]]**\n*theory* - 8 sources\n\nCategories versus dimensions, the evidence for each, and the hybrid approaches now proposed.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 598,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 202,
			"color": "#F2C14E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[ICD-11 versus DSM-5 classification]]**\n*framework* - 9 sources\n\nHow ICD-11 and DSM-5-TR differ in scope, structure and constructs, and why the system must be stated whenever a diagnostic label is used.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 860,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 202,
			"color": "#F2C14E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_3",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Co-occurrence and differential reasoning]]**\n*framework* - 10 sources\n\nWhy co-occurrence is common, what generates it, and how differential reasoning changes when more than one condition is present.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 1122,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 226,
			"color": "#F2C14E"
		},
		{
			"id": "g0",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Description and classification",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 310,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 1078
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_0",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Mood disorders]]**\n*condition* - 7 sources\n\nDepressive and bipolar constructs, their boundaries, and how recurrence and course shape the description.",
			"x": 490,
			"y": 360,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 178,
			"color": "#F2C14E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Anxiety and fear constructs]]**\n*condition* - 7 sources\n\nFear, anxiety and avoidance as constructs, the family of anxiety disorders, and the learning accounts behind exposure treatment.",
			"x": 490,
			"y": 598,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 202,
			"color": "#F2C14E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Psychosis constructs]]**\n*condition* - 8 sources\n\nPsychosis as a symptom domain, the schizophrenia construct, and the dimensional features within it.",
			"x": 490,
			"y": 860,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 178,
			"color": "#F2C14E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_3",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[OCD and related constructs]]**\n*condition* - 8 sources\n\nObsessions and compulsions, the reinforcement cycle, and how the construct is distinguished from anxiety disorders.",
			"x": 490,
			"y": 1098,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 178,
			"color": "#F2C14E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_4",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Dissociative constructs]]**\n*condition* - 9 sources\n\nDissociation as disruption of integrated functions, its place in trauma-related classification, and the assessment problem.",
			"x": 490,
			"y": 1336,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 178,
			"color": "#F2C14E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_5",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Substance-related constructs]]**\n*condition* - 8 sources\n\nSubstance use, dependence and addiction constructs, and the reward and adaptation accounts that describe them.",
			"x": 490,
			"y": 1574,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 178,
			"color": "#F2C14E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_6",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Personality constructs and traits]]**\n*condition* - 7 sources\n\nTrait dimensions and personality disorder constructs, and the dimensional turn in their measurement.",
			"x": 490,
			"y": 1812,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 178,
			"color": "#F2C14E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_7",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Borderline personality disorder]]**\n*condition* - 10 sources\n\nA personality disorder of unstable mood, self-image and relationships: its features and co-occurrence, a course in which symptoms remit while functioning lags, class-level evidence for structured psychotherapies, and the differentials with bipolar II, complex PTSD and autism in women.",
			"x": 490,
			"y": 2050,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 274,
			"color": "#F2C14E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_8",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Eating disorders]]**\n*condition* - 5 sources\n\nAnorexia nervosa, bulimia nervosa, binge-eating disorder and ARFID: prevalence, medical and suicide risk, class-level treatment evidence, and the measured overlap with ADHD and autism.",
			"x": 880,
			"y": 360,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 226,
			"color": "#F2C14E"
		},
		{
			"id": "g1",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Construct families",
			"x": 460,
			"y": 310,
			"width": 810,
			"height": 2054
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_0",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Network and developmental formulations]]**\n*framework* - 8 sources\n\nTwo integrative ways of describing psychopathology: interacting symptoms and developmental pathways.",
			"x": 1340,
			"y": 360,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 202,
			"color": "#F2C14E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Functional outcomes and measurement]]**\n*framework* - 6 sources\n\nFunctioning and participation as outcomes in their own right, the ICF framework, and why symptom change is not the same as life change.",
			"x": 1340,
			"y": 622,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 202,
			"color": "#F2C14E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Emotion dysregulation across conditions]]**\n*framework* - 9 sources\n\nEmotion dysregulation as a transdiagnostic dimension: how it appears and is measured in ADHD, bipolar disorder, autism and complex PTSD, how it differs from mood episodes, and what looks shared or distinct.",
			"x": 1340,
			"y": 884,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 274,
			"color": "#F2C14E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_3",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Suicide and self-harm]]**\n*framework* - 13 sources\n\nSuicidal thoughts, self-harm and suicide across bipolar disorders, ADHD, autism, PTSD and related conditions: what raises group risk, what the risk-factor literature shows, and why predicting any one person's outcome performs poorly.",
			"x": 1340,
			"y": 1218,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 250,
			"color": "#F2C14E"
		},
		{
			"id": "g2",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Formulation and context",
			"x": 1310,
			"y": 310,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 1198
		},
